cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pyanno4rt: python-based advanced numerical nonlinear optimization for radiotherapy"
message: "If you use pyanno4rt in your work, let us now and cite this repository as below."
version: 1.0.0
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Tim"
    family-names: "Ortkamp"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6603-3088"
  - given-names: "Oliver"
    family-names: "Jäkel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6056-9747"
  - given-names: "Martin"
    family-names: "Frank"
  - given-names: "Niklas"
    family-names: "Wahl"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1451-223X"
abstract: "pyanno4rt is a Python package for conventional and outcome prediction model-based inverse photon and proton treatment plan optimization, including radiobiological and machine learning (ML) models for normal tissue complication probability (NTCP) and tumor control probability (TCP). It leverages state-of-the-art local and global solution methods to handle both single- and multi-objective (un)constrained optimization problems in radiotherapy treatment planning."
keywords:
  - python
  - data-science
  - machine-learning
  - optimization
  - outcome-prediction
  - radiotherapy-treatment-planning
